  #line-at(70.824pt, 340.73pt, "The pyrolysis process makes it possible to improve the electronic properties of the RF xerogel ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 361.49pt, "due to the monolithic structure of the resulting carbogel composed of carbon particles linked ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 382.13pt, "by covalent bonds. This means that the electrical conductivity is directly related to the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 402.89pt, "connection between particles. In addition, high temperature treatment further increases the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 423.53pt, "electrical conductivity. This increase can be attributed to the appearance of new layers of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 444.31pt, "graphene as well as lower contact resistances between particles [17]. Due to thermal activation, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 464.95pt, "electrical conductivity is governed by two mechanisms, namely: the movement of charge ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 485.71pt, "carriers along the network of the material by inter-aggregate contact, or a transfer of charge ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 506.35pt, "carriers from one electrically conducting segment of the network to another separated by an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 527.11pt, "amorphous zone. In these cases, an electron hopping mechanism or a tunneling mechanism ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 547.75pt, "allows electrons to cross potential barriers [18, 19]. It should be noted that conduction by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 568.51pt, "tunneling applies when particles are separated by a distance of only a few nanometers. The ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 589.15pt, "conduction electrons can thus pass the energy barrier allowing them to pass from one ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 609.94pt, "conductive particle to another in the polymer matrix. In addition, an increase in temperature ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 630.58pt, "makes it possible to provide additional energy to the electrons, thus promoting conduction ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 651.34pt, "mechanisms by electron hopping and tunneling [20].  These different mechanisms ensure ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 671.98pt, "continuous diffusion of charge carriers, even in the case where there is a break in the links at ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 692.74pt, "the level of the network chains. This, therefore, contributes to a high electrical conductivity by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 713.38pt, "maintaining the so called ‘percolation’ of the system. The theory of percolation explains the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 734.14pt, "percolation phenomenon through several statistical models [21, 22] by dividing it into three ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 754.776pt, "zones (shown in figure 1) as follows: ")
]

