  #line-at(70.824pt, 641.74pt, "in section 2.1. and attributed to the presence of a percolation threshold. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 670.42pt, "On the other hand, for higher doping rates (> 10%), the percolation threshold is exceeded, in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 691.18pt, "addition, the potential barrier is significantly weakened due to the excessively high ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 711.82pt, "concentration of charge carriers, which explains both the stagnation in electrical conductivity ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 732.58pt, "and the reduction in the Seebeck coefficient [28, 30]. Thus, in the continuation of this work, we ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 753.216pt, "didn't persist with higher doping rates - hypothetically making it possible to reach the ")
]

