  #line-at(188.45pt, 300.77pt, "Figure 10: RF xerogel manufacturing process ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 329.45pt, "The advantage of this synthesis process lies in the possibility of formulating RF xerogel plates ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 350.21pt, "with the desired dimensions and shapes, on a large scale, provided that the synthesis parameters ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 370.85pt, "detailed above are respected. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.53pt, "4.2 Heat treatment by pyrolysis ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 428.21pt, "The pyrolysis step allows us to obtain a carbonaceous material via almost total elimination of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 448.99pt, "heteroatoms such as N, O, H or S. It is carried out in a temperature range between 600°C and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 469.63pt, "1200°C under a flow of inert gas to prevent the combustion of the xerogel. At the end of this ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 490.39pt, "process, the carbonizate or carbon xerogel or carbogel obtained is made up of more or less ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 511.03pt, "ordered graphitic crystallites (polyaromatic carbons). During this work, two pyrolysis ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 531.79pt, "temperatures were investigated, 650°C and 850°C. After drying, the gels are pyrolyzed under a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 552.43pt, "stream of nitrogen in a pyrolysis oven with a heating ramp of 1°C min")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(404.74pt, 547.87pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(411.46pt, 552.43pt, " in order to preserve the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 573.19pt, "structure of the xerogel as much as possible. The chosen pyrolysis program also includes ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 593.83pt, "isotherm stages, namely a 1-hour stage at 140°C to ensure that all the water molecules absorbed ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 614.62pt, "on the surface are evaporated, then a second 30 min stage at 140°C, final temperature before ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 635.26pt, "cooling under nitrogen to room temperature. Note that beyond 600°C the CH2 type bonds as ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 656.02pt, "well as the -CH2 -O-CH2 - bridges are eliminated [77]. The steps of one of our pyrolysis ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 676.66pt, "programs is illustrated in figure 11. ")
]

