  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 180.86pt, "Developing the complex architecture of TEGs with carbogels is challenging due to its fragility. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 201.5pt, "We addressed this challenge by developing the modules with a single type of material (p-type). ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 222.26pt, "The loss of yield caused by avoiding junctions with two types of materials (n-type and p-type), ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 242.9pt, "was compensated by our ability to design modules with a large size of 30 cm which otherwise ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 263.69pt, "is difficult for usual commercial materials due to their complexity of synthesis and greater ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 284.33pt, "rigidity. Another reason for this choice is to retain the primary super-insulating function of the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 305.09pt, "material by obviating the need for thermal bridges, hence, avoiding the increase in thermal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 325.73pt, "conductivity and the weakening of the material. To establish the electrical contact, two copper ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 346.49pt, "plates (supplied by GoodFellow) of 50 µm thickness were soldered with ultra-thin (<250 µm) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 367.13pt, "flat copper electrical cable and covered with an adhesive that can withstand a temperature of up ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 387.89pt, "to 90°C. Then, in order to allow the module to be placed under vacuum while protecting the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 408.53pt, "material and avoiding short circuits, we used a pocket of electrical insulating film (supplied by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 429.29pt, "Rexor), transversely covering the entire material and leaving the passage for the electrical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 449.95pt, "output cables. Lastly, the material was placed under vacuum in a waterproof envelop- ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 470.59pt, "thermoelectric vacuum insulation panel (TVIP)- to further reduce the thermal conductivity (< ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 491.35pt, "15 mW.m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.7pt, 486.79pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.42pt, 491.35pt, ".K")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.06pt, 486.79pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(143.78pt, 491.35pt, ") as well as contact resistance for allowing the participation of the material with ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 511.99pt, "entire surface roughness in the electricity generation. The welding was carried out by the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 532.75pt, "vacuum machine at more than 100°C that melted the adhesive around the cable, making it ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 553.39pt, "possible to obtain a homogeneous and waterproof weld all around the copper electrical cable. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 574.15pt, "The end of the two copper cables outside the casing is then connected to the initial electrical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 594.79pt, "cables in order to facilitate the use of the module.  The following figure represents the different ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 615.58pt, "elements constituting the TVIP (figure 12). A sealing test was conducted to confirm the vacuum ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 636.22pt, "retention of the TVIPs by comparing the evolution of the pressure in the envelope containing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 656.98pt, "the thermoelectric module using standard electrical cables (leading to a rapid loss of vacuum) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 677.62pt, "and that in the envelope with the thermoelectric module using electrical cables with a thickness ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 698.38pt, "of 250 µm. The results are presented in figure S3 and discussed in supplementary methods in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 719.02pt, "section S2.2 of the SI. After fabricating the TVIP (see fig. S4), it is also necessary to create an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 739.78pt, "operational test bench and delineate the formalism to evaluate the performance of Seebeck ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 760.416pt, "effect TE modules. This is discussed in section S1.3 and S1.4 in the SI. ")
]

